messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D.\n####\n# Context:\nAt present, there are still a large number of bricklayers, steel bar workers, boiler workers, painters and other types of blue-collar jobs in our country, but under the influence of professional disciplinization, only relevant ones can be found in the professional catalogue of secondary vocational education in our country. and all with a strong discipline color of professional names. These professional names make it difficult for students to match future jobs with the above-mentioned blue-collar jobs, resulting in a big discount for graduates who actually enter the above-mentioned blue-collar jobs.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following options is intended to be pointed out in this paragraph?\n# Options:\nA) The major catalogue of secondary vocational education in china needs to be adjusted according to the actual post demand.\nB) The professional education of secondary vocational education in china is unable to train students to enter blue-collar posts.\nC) Bricklayer, steel bar worker, boiler worker and other posts are not blue-collar jobs in the traditional sense.\nD) The disconnection between the setting of professional names and the actual educational content makes it difficult for secondary vocational school students to obtain employment.. I think the correct option is: C\n', "<think>Okay, let's tackle this problem. So, the context is talking about how there are a lot of blue-collar jobs like bricklayers, steel workers, etc., but in secondary vocational education, the professional catalogues have names that are too discipline-oriented. Because of these names, students can't easily connect their studies to the actual jobs, leading to fewer graduates actually entering those blue-collar roles.\n\nThe question is asking which option the paragraph is pointing out. Let's look at the options one by one.\n\nOption A says the major catalog needs adjustment based on actual job demand. The paragraph mentions that the current names are too disciplinary and don't align with the actual jobs, so adjusting the catalog to match real job titles makes sense here. That could be the right answer.\n\nOption B claims that vocational education can't train students for blue-collar jobs. But the problem isn't the training itself; it's the naming of the majors. The students might have the skills but can't see the connection because of the names. So B might be too extreme.\n\nOption C suggests those jobs aren't traditional blue-collar. The paragraph says they are blue-collar jobs, so C is probably wrong.\n\nOption D talks about a disconnect between professional names and educational content. The issue here is more about the names not matching the job titles, not the content. The paragraph doesn't mention the content being disconnected, just the naming. So D might not be correct. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
