go. Since Lin Xi went, the temperature cannot be very low (\u00acR). However, this does not necessarily mean the temperature is very high; it could be moderate. Thus, B is not necessarily true.\n\n- **Option C (The wind is strong)**: The context does not mention wind at all, so this is irrelevant. Thus, C cannot be inferred.\n\n- **Option D (The sky is clear)**: The third statement (Q \u2192 S) directly states that if Lin Xi went (Q), then the sky must be clear (S). Since Q is true, S must also be true. Therefore, D is a valid inference.\n\nThe correct answer is \\boxed{D}.",
