messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D.\n####\n# Context:\nRecently, researchers have discovered that fever can promote the transfer of lymphocytes to the site of infection. They explained that this is because fever increases the expression of heat shock protein 90 (Hsp90) in T lymphocytes, this protein binds to integrins , T lymphocytes adhere to blood vessels and eventually accelerate their migration to the site of infection.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following, can best support the above discussion?\n# Options:\nA) Integrin is a cell adhesion molecule that can control the transport of t lymphocytes during fever\nB) Fever can induce hsp90 to bind to the tail of integrin and activate integrin\nC) Not only fever, other pressure can also induce the expression of hsp90 in t lymphocytes\nD) After hsp90 binds to integrin, it can activate the signaling pathway that promotes the migration of t lymphocytes. I think the correct option is: A\n', '<think>Okay, let\'s tackle this question. So the context is about how fever helps in moving lymphocytes to infection sites by increasing Hsp90 in T cells, which then bind to integrins, leading to adhesion and migration. The question is asking which option best supports this discussion.\n\nFirst, I need to recall the given information. The key points are: fever → more Hsp90 in T cells → Hsp90 binds integrins → T cells stick to blood vessels → migrate to infection. .\n\nNow, looking at the options:.\n\nOption A says integrin is a cell adhesion molecule that controls T cell transport during fever. The context does mention integrin\'s role in adhesion, but does it specifically say that integrin controls the transport during fever? The passage states that Hsp90 binds integrins, leading to adhesion. So maybe A is part of the process but is it the best support?.\n\nOption B: Fever induces Hsp90 to bind to the 