tment have never called others**. The contrapositive of this is: *If someone made a call, they must have answered at least one call from another member of the department*.\n\n### Evaluation of Options:\n- **Option A**: \"Xiao Zhao never answered a phone call from Xiao Li.\"  \n  Xiao Li called Xiao Zhao, but there is no information about whether Xiao Zhao answered. Since Xiao Zhao never made any calls, this does not violate Statement 3. However, we cannot confirm whether he answered or not. **This cannot be inferred.**\n\n- **Option B**: \"Xiao Li once answered a phone call from Xiao Wang.\"  \n  Xiao Wang called everyone, so Xiao Li must have received a call from Xiao Wang. Since Xiao Li made a call to Xiao Zhao (Statement 2), he must have answered at least one call from another member (per Statement 3). The only possible call Xiao Li could have answered is from Xiao Wang (since Xiao Zhao never called anyone). Therefore, Xiao Li **must have answered Xiao Wang\u2019s call**. **This can be inferred.**\n\n- **Option C**: \"Someone in the administration department once called Xiao Wang.\"  \n  Xiao Wang called everyone, but there is no information that others called him. Xiao Li only called Zhao, and Xiao Zhao made no calls. Without additional members mentioned, this cannot be confirmed. **This cannot be inferred.**\n\n- **Option D**: \"Xiao Wang answered the phone from everyone in the administration department.\"  \n  The problem does not state that others called Xiao Wang. Xiao Wang initiated calls but there is no evidence he received calls from everyone. **This cannot be inferred.**\n\n### Conclusion:\nThe only logically consistent inference is **Option B**.\n\n**Answer:** B) Xiao Li once answered a phone call from Xiao Wang.",
