excluded**.\n\n3. **Zhang and Zhou must attend**: Constraint 4 requires two of Zhang, Sun, Zhou to attend. Since Sun is out, Zhang and Zhou must both attend.\n\n4. **Wang and Li\u2019s status**:  \n   - If **Li attends**, Wang must also attend (constraint 5).  \n   - If **Li doesn\u2019t attend**, Wang also doesn\u2019t attend.  \n\n   This creates two valid scenarios:  \n   - **Scenario 1**: Zhang, Zhou, Li, Wang attend.  \n   - **Scenario 2**: Only Zhang and Zhou attend.  \n\n### Analysis of Options:\n- **A) Zhang and Wang**: Zhang is always present (required by constraints 3 and 4). Thus, Zhang cannot be excluded, making this pair impossible.  \n- **B) Wang and Li**: They can attend together (Scenario 1) or not (Scenario 2). Not guaranteed to be excluded.  \n- **C) Li and Zhao**: Zhao is always excluded, but Li may attend in Scenario 1. Not guaranteed to be excluded.  \n- **D) Zhao and Sun**: Both are excluded in **all valid scenarios** due to the constraints.  \n\n**Correct Answer**: **D (Zhao and Sun)**. They are definitively excluded in every valid case.",
