terprises cannot utilize the RMB settlement service, rendering the risk-avoidance benefit moot. \n\n**Option B** addresses this critical prerequisite by specifying that overseas enterprises are willing to use RMB, particularly due to its stable value. While the stability of RMB is not explicitly mentioned in the context, the core requirement is the willingness of overseas partners to adopt RMB. This makes **B** the necessary assumption for the argument's validity. \n\nOther options (A, C, D) focus on increased trade volume, ease of trade, or market size, which are tangential to the core issue of exchange rate risk mitigation through RMB settlement. Thus, **B** is the best answer.\n\n<\uff5cAnswer\uff5c>B<\uff5c/Answer\uff5c>",
