ry buildings, high land value areas (where land is expensive and construction must maximize vertical space) would require steel or concrete for taller structures. Since bamboo is unsuitable for such buildings, it becomes economically inferior in these areas. \n\n**Why other options are less likely:**\n- **B** (preservatives cost) doesn't directly tie to high land values.\n- **C** (bamboo cleared for construction) might reduce availability but doesn\u2019t explain why bamboo is *economically inferior* in high-value areas (it could still be cheaper if available).\n- **D** (earthquake resistance) is irrelevant to the economic exception.\n\n**A** directly links high land values (needing multistory buildings) to bamboo's inadequacy, explaining why it isn\u2019t economically viable there. \n\n**Answer:** A",
