th is invalid. \n\nPerhaps table1\'s pair is Zhao and someone else. \n\nLet me try:\n\nTable1\'s pair is Zhao and a girl (not Zhang, since Zhang must be with Lu). \n\nSuppose table1\'s girl is Shi Lin (but she was at table2 earlier). \n\nThis is getting too complex. Given time constraints, I\'ll proceed with the best possible answer. \n\nThe only player who must have tied is Yang Hong at table4 if she\'s there with someone else, but that violates condition3. \n\nAlternatively, Zhang Fang could have a tie in her games (at table1 with Lu Wei), which would satisfy condition2 (table1 has a tie). \n\nThus, the answer might be C) Zhang Fang or D) Fan Yong. \n\nLooking back, if the pair at table1 has a tie, Zhang Fang could have one tie. \n\nAlternatively, Fan at table3 could have two ties. \n\nBut since the question asks which one "made a tie with the opponent", and the options include Fan Yong (D), who could have ties in his games, I\'ll go with D) Fan Yong. \n\nWait, but earlier analysis suggested that if Fan has a 4-2 difference, he could have two ties and a win. Thus, he did tie, so D is possible. \n\nAlternatively, Zhang Fang\'s pair (5-1) could have a tie. \n\nIf the pair has5-1 with a tie, then one of them tied a game. \n\nFor example, Zhang has5 (2 wins and 1 tie) and Lu has1 (1 tie and 2 losses). Thus, Zhang tied once. \n\nSo option C is possible. \n\nBetween C and D. \n\nBut let\'s see condition (3): Zhao\'s pair has no ties. \n\nIf Zhao is at table3 with Wang Yu (4-2), and they have no ties, that\'s okay. \n\nFan at table3 would be if he\'s leading. \n\nWait, in my previous scenario where table3 is Fan and Wang with4-2 (Fan4, Wang2), Fan has two wins and one tie (4=2+2+0? No. 2+2=4 from two wins, no tie. Or one win and two ties: 2+1+1=4. Then he has two ties. Thus, he tied. \n\nThus, Fan has two ties, so he made a tie. \n\nTherefore, D) Fan Yong is a candidate. \n\nZhang Fang also tied once. \n\nBut the question says "if one of the following players made a tie..", so possibly multiple could, but we need the correct option. \n\nLooking back at the conditions:\n\nCondition (4) says Fan is leading his opponent. If his score is4-2, he is leading, and he did tie games. \n\nThus, Fan Yong (D) made a tie. \n\nAlternatively, Zhang Fang also did. \n\nBut the problem might have only one correct answer. \n\nLet me check the options again:\n\nOptions:\n\nA) Shi Lin: If she\'s at table2 (paired with Li Long), but Li has0, she has6, so no ties. \n\nB) Yang Hong: If she\'s at4 with3-3, she tied all games. But if paired with someone like Fan, he can\'t be leading. \n\nC) Zhang Fang: If she has5 points with a tie, yes. \n\nD) Fan Yong: If he has4 with two ties, yes. \n\nThe question asks "if one of the following..", so the correct answer is likely D) Fan Yong, as the conditions allow it and he\'s leading. \n\nBut I\'m not entirely sure. However, given the analysis, I\'ll choose D.\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']] 15%|#5        | 90/600 [32:51<2:44:42, 19.38s/it]
