inability, then success implies having training).  \n- **B** is logically sound (lacking a required credential makes practice illegal).  \n- **C** assumes a causal chain without fallacy (coffee \u2192 jittery \u2192 unsuitable for certain jobs).  \n\n**Correct Answer: D**",
