D) Temple of heaven, temple of heaven, imperial palace.\n\nYes, so B is Forb, Tian, Tian.\n\nSo the correct answer is B.\n\nBut the user initially thought it was A. Maybe I made a mistake?\n\nWait, let me check Option A's validity again.\n\nOption A's correct answers: Temp, Forb, Temp.\n\nLet's check Candidate 2 (all Tian):.\n\nQ1: Tian vs Temp (wrong),\n\nQ2: Tian vs Forb (wrong),\n\nQ3: Tian vs Temp (wrong). All wrong. Thus, Option A invalid.\n\nCandidate 3 (all Forb):\n\nQ1 Forb vs Temp (wrong),\n\nQ2 Forb vs Forb (correct),\n\nQ3 Forb vs Temp (wrong). So okay.\n\nCandidate 4: Temp (Q1), Tian (Q2), and maybe Forb (Q3).\n\nQ1 correct (Temp), so okay.\n\nCandidate 5: Assuming their answers are Tian (Q1), Forb (Q2), and maybe Forb (Q3).\n\nQ1: wrong,\n\nQ2: correct,\n\nQ3: Forb vs Temp (wrong). So at least one.\n\nCandidate 6: Forb (Q1), Tian (Q2), Forb (Q3).\n\nQ1 Forb vs Temp (wrong),\n\nQ2 Tian vs Forb (wrong),\n\nQ3 Forb vs Temp (wrong). All wrong here. Oh no!.\n\nWait, candidate 6's answers under Option A's correct answers (Temp, Forb, Temp):\n\nTheir answers: Forb (Q1), Tian (Q2), Forb (Q3).\n\nSo:\n\nQ1: Forb vs Temp (wrong),\n\nQ2: Tian vs Forb (wrong),\n\nQ3: Forb vs Temp (wrong). So all wrong. So Option A also fails for candidate 6.\n\nTherefore, Option A is invalid.\n\nThus, the only valid option is B.\n</think>\n\nThe problem requires determining the correct order of answers to three questions about Beijing's scenic spots, given that each candidate has at least one correct answer. \n\n**Key Steps:**\n1. **Parse Candidates' Answers:**\n   - **Candidate 1:** [Temple of Heaven (Q1), Temple of Heaven (Q2), Tiananmen Square (Q3)]\n   - **Candidate 2:** [Tiananmen Square (Q1), Tiananmen Square (Q2), Tiananmen Square (Q3)]\n   - **Candidate 3:** [Forbidden City (Q1), Forbidden City (Q2), Forbidden City (Q3)]\n   - **Candidate 4:** [Temple of Heaven (Q1), Tiananmen Square (Q2), assumed Tiananmen Square (Q3)]\n   - **Candidate 5:** [Tiananmen Square (Q1), Forbidd