not address the causal link.\n\n- **Option D** points out that physics laureates also live long but haven\u2019t won economics Nobels. While this suggests Nobel laureates in general might live longer, it does not specifically refute the expert\u2019s claim about economics. The survivorship bias in **A** is a more direct refutation.\n\n**Correct Answer: A**  \nThe expert\u2019s conclusion is weakened by the selection bias in the data: laureates must survive to win, so their longevity precedes the prize. This invalidates the causal inference.",
