e and technology\". Wait, but the 'new world' is in economic growth, not science/tech. Maybe the answer is A, since it's general and captures the ongoing potential. \n\nAlternatively, perhaps the answer is B. Wait, the question might be in Chinese, so maybe there's a nuance. The original Chinese might have wording that matches one of these better. \n\nAlternatively, the first sentence says \"opening up a new world of economic growth\", so the closest option is B which mentions \"brings a new world of science and technology\". But that's not exactly the same. \n\nHmm. Maybe the correct answer is A. Alternatively, the user's initial thought was C. Let me check the options again.\n\nThe question asks for the most suitable title. The passage's main points are:\n\n- Innovation-driven strategy enhances capabilities, fuels high-quality development, opens new economic growth areas.\n\n- During the epidemic, innovation's value was evident through tech applications (vaccines, big data, telework, etc.), which not only helped overcome the crisis but also changed social life.\n\nSo the title needs to encapsulate both the ongoing role in economic growth and the societal impact. \n\nOption C mentions affecting social life, but misses the economic aspect. Option B mentions science/tech's new world, but the main focus is on economic growth and societal impact. \n\nOption A's \"contains unlimited potential\" could cover both the existing contributions and future possibilities, which aligns with \"continuously injecting new momentum\". \n\nAlternatively, the correct answer might be A. But I'm a bit confused because the user initially thought C. \n\nAlternatively, the last sentence says that the changes affected social production and life, so the societal aspect is emphasized. Maybe the best title is C, but that's only part. \n\nAlternatively, the first part of the passage is about economic growth and innovation's role there, so the title should also include that. Since none of the options combine both, perhaps the best is A because it's broader. \n\nAlternatively, the correct answer is B: \"innovation-driven brings a new world of science and technology\" but the passage mentions economic growth, not sci/tech world. \n\nHmm, this is tough. Maybe the answer is A.\n</think>\n\nThe passage highlights the role of innovation-driven development in enhancing economic growth and adapting to challenges like the pandemic, emphasizing both technological advancements and their societal impacts. While the title must encapsulate these elements, **Option A (\"Innovation drive contains unlimited potential\")** best captures the overarching theme. The text underscores innovation's continuous contribution to growth (\"injecting new momentum\") and its adaptability during crises, suggesting inherent potential beyond immediate applications. Other options focus narrowly on specific aspects (e.g., social life, science/tech) or misalign with the emphasis on economic and societal impacts. \n\n**Answer:** A) Innovation drive contains unlimited potential",
