" making **B consistent** with the text.  \n- **Option C**: While the text specifies lasers are \"widely used in communication technology,\" the phrase \"broad application prospect of science and technology\" could be inferred from the description of laser technology as a \"high and new technology\" with notable properties (e.g., high energy concentration, monochromaticity). Though not explicitly stated, this option aligns with the text\u2019s tone of technological potential.  \n- **Option D**: The text **never mentions** anything about subverting traditional optical theory. The discussion focuses on characteristics (brightness, temperature, monochromaticity) and applications (communication), but there is no reference to challenging or\u98a0\u8986ing existing theories. This makes **D inconsistent** with the text.  \n\nThus, **D** is the correct answer as it introduces an idea not supported by the context.",
