      "text": " D.\n</think>\n\nThe context states that men who underwent the same surgery and took the same painkillers experienced **less pain relief** and that the painkillers were \"**less effective for less time**\" compared to women. This indicates two key findings:  \n1. **Lower effectiveness**: Painkillers provided men with weaker pain relief.  \n2. **Shorter duration**: The painkillers\u2019 effectiveness lasted a shorter time for men.  \n\n### Analysis of Options:\n- **A)** Incorrect. The text does not claim painkillers are entirely ineffective for men. Men still experienced some relief, just less than women.  \n- **B)** Partially true but incomplete. While the shorter duration implies pain returned sooner for men, this option focuses only on timing. The text also emphasizes *less pain relief* (not just duration), making this an incomplete interpretation.  \n- **C)** Irrelevant. The study addresses painkiller efficacy, not pain tolerance. There is no mention of men\u2019s ability to endure pain.  \n- **D)** Correct. The phrase \"works better for women\" directly captures both findings: painkillers provided stronger relief and lasted longer in women. This is the most comprehensive and accurate restatement of the text.  \n\n### Answer:\n**D) The same painkiller works better for women than for men.**",
