Zhang Hua > year before last).  \n- **Issue**: The premise is a **specific comparison** (\"this year\u2019s performance is better than the year before last\"), not a general principle. This differs from the original\u2019s universal premise.  \n\n**D)**  \n- **Structure**: General premise (quality + advertising \u2192 demand), comparison (Company A > Company B in advertising), conclusion (A\u2019s demand > B\u2019s).  \n- **Issue**: The premise requires **two factors** (quality and advertising), but the conclusion only addresses one. This introduces a flaw absent in the original.  \n\n### Conclusion:  \n**Option B** most closely mirrors the original reasoning because it uses a **universal premise with a direct, factual relationship** and applies it to a **specific comparison** to derive a valid conclusion.  \n\n**Answer: B**",
