hat deforestation caused food shortages and collapse, thereby strengthening the experts' position. \n\nOther options:  \n- **A** supports the traditional view by detailing tree-cutting activities.  \n- **C** reinforces the timeline of deforestation, aligning with the original theory.  \n- **D** introduces colonization as a later cause, but the traditional decline is typically attributed to pre-colonial events. Since **B** directly addresses the link between deforestation and societal collapse, it is the strongest choice.  \n\n**Answer:** B",
