messages:  [["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D.\n####\n# Context:\nIntuitive thinking refers to the thinking in which the behavior steps and thinking process are not clear and clear, and some guesses, assumptions or judgments are made directly and quickly about some phenomena or problems.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following is typical intuitive thinking?\n# Options:\nA) The public security and criminal police analyzed the case according to the evidence collected\nB) Military commanders make military decisions based on the intelligence materials of the scouts\nC) Solve the problems in the exam based on the knowledge learned\nD) The doctor quickly made a diagnosis of the disease based on the patient's oral materials. I think the correct option is: B\n", '<think>Okay, let\'s see. The question is about identifying which option is an example of intuitive thinking as defined here. The definition says intuitive thinking involves unclear steps, guesses, assumptions, or quick judgments without clear processes.\n\nLooking at the options:.\n\nA) Public security analyzing cases with evidence. That sounds more methodical, using evidence, so maybe not intuitive.\n\nB) Military commanders using scout intelligence. They base decisions on data, so also analytical, not quick guesses?.\n\nC) Solving exam problems with learned knowledge. That\'s applying learned methods, so structured, not intuitive.\n\nD) Doctor quickly diagnosing from patient\'s info. Hmm, doctors might use quick judgment, especially if they\'re experienced, making a snap diagnosis without all steps laid out. That fits the intuitive thinking description because it\'s a rapid judgment based on available info without a clear, step-by-step process.\n\nWait, but sometimes doctors follow protocols. But the key here is "quickly made a diagnosis based on oral materials. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
