ls out the wall clock\u2019s advancement relative to standard time. Thus, the watch keeps perfect time.  \n\n**Why Other Options Are Incorrect**:  \n- **A**: The watch\u2019s correctness isn\u2019t due to it being new; it\u2019s due to the error cancellation.  \n- **C**: The inference is logically valid; no ambiguity exists.  \n- **D**: The errors are equivalent in magnitude and opposite in direction, so they cancel out.  \n\n**Answer**: B",
