s obsolescence.\n\n3. **Option D** (mentioned as the user's guess) is irrelevant because it discusses shelf-space costs, which do not directly link to the disappearance of old-style detergents.\n\nWhile both **A** and **C** are strong, **C** is the stronger choice because it directly ties the manufacturers' decision (to reduce cardboard) to consumer preferences. The environmental angle aligns with the manufacturers' reasoning, creating a synergistic effect that ensures old-style detergents become obsolete due to declining demand. **A**, while valid, focuses on supply-side constraints, which are less immediately impactful than consumer-driven demand shifts.\n\n**Answer:** C",
