ge focuses on the necessity of policies, not detailed methods.  \n- **C** (\"explain characteristics of the economic situation\") is too narrow; while the passage mentions the global division of labor and differential impacts, its core argument is about policy responses.  \n- **D** (\"differential industrial regulation\") is close but less precise than B, as it emphasizes \"regulation and control\" rather than the **specificity and targeting** of policies explicitly stated in the text.  \n\n**Answer: B**",
