t be concluded. The problem does not provide enough information about the number of employees in each role. The overall average being lower than both dieticians and PTs implies the presence of lower-paid employees outside these roles, but the relative numbers of dieticians vs. PTs are not determinable.\n\n- **Options A and C** are also invalid. A dietician could earn below $42,000 (since their average is $50,000), and a dietician\u2019s salary need not exceed the highest-paid PT\u2019s salary (e.g., PT salaries could range with a high near $50,000 while averaging $42,000).\n\nThus, **B** is the only conclusion that logically follows. \n\n**Answer:** B",
