tial thought was A, which is incorrect. \n\nTherefore, the answer should be B.\n</think>\n\nTo determine David's choice, we compare the annual salaries from both companies over time:\n\n**Huizhong's Salary Structure:**\n- **First Half-Year:** $500,000\n- **Each Subsequent Half-Year:** Increases by $50,000.\n\n**Annual Calculations for Huizhong:**\n- **Year 1:** $500,000 (1st half) + $550,000 (2nd half) = **$1,050,000**  \n- **Year 2:** $600,000 (3rd half) + $650,000 (4th half) = **$1,250,000**  \n- **Year 3:** $700,000 (5th half) + $750,000 (6th half) = **$1,450,000**  \n- **Annual Increase for Huizhong:** $200,000/year (e.g., $1,050k \u2192 $1,250k in Year 2).  \n\n**Cantor's Salary Structure:**\n- **Annual Salary:** Starts at $1,000,000, increasing by $200,000 annually.\n\n**Annual Calculations for Cantor:**\n- **Year 1:** **$1,000,000**  \n- **Year 2:** **$1,200,000**  \n- **Year 3:** **$1,400,000**  \n- **Annual Increase for Cantor:** $200,000/year.  \n\n**Comparison:**  \n- **Year 1:** Huizhong ($1,050,000) vs. Cantor ($1,000,000) \u2192 **+50,000 for Huizhong**.  \n- **Year 2:** Huizhong ($1,250,000) vs. Cantor ($1,200,000) \u2192 **+50,000 for Huizhong**.  \n- **Year 3:** Huizhong ($1,450,000) vs. Cantor ($1,400,000) \u2192 **+50,000 for Huizhong**.  \n\nThe **difference remains consistent at $50,000 annually** for Huizhong over Cantor.  \n\n**Analysis of Options:**  \n- **A (Cantor, $150,000 extra in 2 years):** Incorrect. Huizhong earns **$100,000 more** over two years.  \n- **B (Huizhong, $50,000 extra annually):** Correct. Matches the consistent annual difference.  \n- **C (Cantor, $50,000 extra annually):** Incorrect. Cantor is always behind.  \n- **D (Huizhong, $70,000 extra annually):** Incorrect. The difference is **$50,000**, not $70,000.  \n\n**Correct Answer:** **B** (David will go to Huizhong because he will get an extra $50,000 a year).  \n\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>  \n**Answer:** B",
