ng, aligning with the paragraph\u2019s emphasis on memory, analysis, and reflection.  \n- **B** is broader but less precise. While the method of reception does affect behavior (e.g., changing channels), the paragraph\u2019s core argument centers on cognitive processes.  \n- **C** is unsupported; the text does not claim TV causes \"wrong values,\" only that viewers avoid conflicting perspectives.  \n- **D** introduces temperament (calmness), which is never mentioned.  \n\nThe strongest conclusion is that **text facilitates better thinking than TV**, making **A** the correct answer.\n\n**Answer:** A) Reading text is more helpful for thinking than watching TV.",
