d maintenance).\n   - **D**: A software company develops a system for an enterprise. Development by an external entity qualifies as outsourcing under the definition.\n\n3. **Key Distinction for B**: While other options explicitly involve an enterprise outsourcing to an external party, **B** describes a generic operator improving its own software for \"customers\" without specifying an enterprise\u2019s systems. This makes it an example of general service improvement rather than a specific outsourcing arrangement. \n\nThus, **B** does not belong to information system outsourcing as defined. \n\n**Answer:** B",
