    {
      "index": 0,
      "text": " C\n</think>\n\nThe correct answer is **C) For the sake of future generations, we must adhere to the scientific outlook on development.**\n\n### Reasoning:\n1. **First premise**: \"Only by adhering to the scientific outlook on development can we achieve sustainable development.\"  \n   This establishes that adhering to the scientific outlook (**A**) is a **necessary condition** for achieving sustainable development (**B**). Logically, this translates to **B \u2192 A** (if sustainable development is achieved, then the scientific outlook was followed).\n\n2. **Second premise**: \"We must achieve sustainable development for the sake of future generations.\"  \n   This states that achieving sustainable development (**B**) is **required** because of future generations.  \n\n3. **Inference**:  \n   Since sustainable development (**B**) is necessary for future generations, and **A** (adhering to the scientific outlook) is a prerequisite for **B**, it follows that adhering to the scientific outlook (**A**) is also necessary for future generations. This directly leads to **C**, which combines the necessity of the scientific outlook with the goal of future generations.  \n\n### Why other options are incorrect:\n- **A) Increase publicity**: No mention of publicity or awareness campaigns in the premises. Irrelevant.  \n- **B) Scientific management**: The context refers to the \"scientific outlook,\" not \"scientific management,\" making this a stretch.  \n- **D) \"As long as...\" implies sufficiency**: The premise states that adhering to the scientific outlook is **necessary**, not that it guarantees sustainable development. This misrepresents the logical relationship.  \n\nThus, **C** is the only valid inference.",
