      "text": " C\n</think>\n\nThe context specifies that in the countryside, only boys historically had the right to study. Since Zhang Fei successfully entered university, this implies they had access to education, which under the given conditions would require being a boy. Additionally, overcoming the rural background to achieve university entry suggests familial support, as families typically invest in their children's education when they value them. \n\n**Option C** directly addresses the gender requirement (being a boy) and the implied familial support (\"valued by the family\"), both of which are logically inferred from the context. \n\nOther options fail because:  \n- **A** (good parent relationship) is not mentioned.  \n- **B** (mindset/openness to new ideas) is speculative and not tied to the gender-based barrier.  \n- **D** (a girl) contradicts the premise that girls were historically denied education.  \n\n**Answer: C**",
