perlatives like \"most developed\" are unsupported here.\n\n4. **Option D**: The text states the Yuan \"actively carried out overseas trade,\" but it does **not** claim they had \"the most prosperous overseas trade in history.\" The Song Dynasty, for instance, is historically noted for thriving maritime trade, and the mention of Zheng He\u2019s later voyages implies Ming-era developments. Thus, D overreaches the text\u2019s claims.\n\n### Conclusion:\nThe only option directly supported by the text is **A**, as it aligns with the explicit comparison of the Yuan\u2019s expanded geographic contacts.",
