\'t vote for them), so Li Zilu must vote for all. Therefore, Li Zilu voted for everyone, including Wang Ming. So Li Zilu definitely voted for Wang Ming.\n\nNow, what about Wang Ming\'s vote for Li Zilu?\n\nWang Ming\'s condition: he checked all those who checked Zhao Jie. Let\'s parse this again. Suppose "those" refers to candidates. So, if a candidate was checked by someone who checked Zhao Jie, then Wang Ming must check that candidate. Wait, that might make sense. Let me rephrase:\n\nIf any voter checked both Zhao Jie and another candidate X, then Wang Ming must check candidate X. Additionally, since those voters checked Zhao Jie, Wang Ming must check Zhao Jie as well. Wait, maybe it\'s that Wang Ming votes for every candidate that was co-voted with Zhao Jie by any voter. Or perhaps Wang Ming votes for Zhao Jie and any other candidate that was voted for by any voter who voted for Zhao Jie.\n\nAlternatively, the wording could mean that Wang Ming votes for all the candidates that were selected by any voter who selected Zhao Jie. So, for example, if a voter votes for Zhao Jie and Wang Ming, then Wang Ming must vote for Zhao Jie and Wang Ming (himself). If another voter votes for Zhao Jie and Li Zilu, then Wang Ming must vote for Li Zilu as well. Therefore, Wang Ming\'s votes include Zhao Jie plus any other candidates that were paired with Zhao Jie by any voter.\n\nNow, since Li Zilu votes for everyone (because no candidate has a full vote), that means Li Zilu voted for Zhao Jie, Wang Ming, and himself (assuming he\'s a candidate). Therefore, Li Zilu\'s vote includes Wang Ming. So, if Li Zilu voted for Wang Ming, then that means there exists a voter (Li Zilu himself) who voted for Zhao Jie and Wang Ming. Therefore, according to Wang Ming\'s condition, Wang Ming must have voted for Wang Ming (since that voter Li Zilu voted for both Zhao Jie and Wang Ming). Wait, but Li Zilu voted for Zhao Jie as well? Since Li Zilu votes for everyone, yes, he voted for Zhao Jie and Wang Ming and himself.\n\nTherefore, since there is a voter (Li Zilu) who voted for Zhao Jie and Wang Ming, Wang Ming must vote for Wang Ming (himself). Additionally, since Li Zilu also voted for Li Zilu (assuming he\'s a candidate), then if Li Zilu is a candidate, then Wang Ming would have to vote for Li Zilu because Li Zilu (as a voter) voted for Zhao Jie and Li Zilu. Therefore, Wang Ming must vote for Li Zilu.\n\nWait, this would mean that Wang Ming does vote for Li Zilu. Since Li Zilu voted for both Zhao Jie and Li Zilu, then Wang Ming must include Li Zilu in his votes. Therefore, Wang Ming voted for Li Zilu.\n\nBut Li Zilu also voted for Wang Ming, so they did tick each other. That would make option B correct. However, let me check again.\n\nWait, let me step through this carefully.\n\nAssume the candidates are Zhao Jie (ZJ), Wang Ming (WM), and Li Zilu (LZ). So they are all candidates and voters.\n\nLi Zilu\'s votes: since no candidate can have a full vote (because Zhang Hao didn\'t vote), Li Zilu must vote for all three candidates (ZJ, WM, LZ).\n\nTherefore, Li Zilu\'s ballot has all three checked.\n\nNow, Wang Ming\'s condition: he must check all those (candidates) who were checked by those who checked Zhao Jie. So any candidate that was voted for by someone who also voted for Zhao Jie must be included in Wang Ming\'s votes.\n\nSince Li Zilu voted for Zhao Jie and Wang Ming and Li Zilu himself, then Wang Ming must include all three candidates (because Li Zilu checked ZJ and also WM and LZ). Therefore, Wang Ming must check all three candidates as well.\n\nAdditionally, any other voters (apart from Zhang Hao, WM, and LZ) might have voted for ZJ and others, but even without considering them, since Li Zilu\'s vote includes ZJ and the others, Wang Ming must vote for all three.\n\nTherefore, Wang Ming\'s votes include Li Zilu, and Li Zilu\'s votes include Wang Ming. So they did tick each other, which would make option B correct.\n\nWait, but let me check if there\'s any possibility that Wang Ming didn\'t vote for Li Zilu. Suppose that no one except Li Zilu voted for Li Zilu along with Zhao Jie. Then, since Li Zilu did vote for both ZJ and LZ, Wang Ming must include LZ in his votes. Therefore, Wang Ming must have voted for Li Zilu. Hence, they both voted for each other. So option B.\n\nBut let me check another angle. Suppose there\'s another voter, say "Other", who voted only for Zhao Jie. Then, Wang Ming must vote for Zhao Jie, but since that\'s the only candidate that "Other" voted for, Wang Ming doesn\'t have to vote for others unless others also voted for ZJ and other candidates. However, since Li Zilu did vote for ZJ and others, Wang Ming is required to vote for all of them. So regardless of others, as long as Li Zilu voted for ZJ and WM and LZ, Wang must include them all.\n\nTherefore, Wang Ming votes for LZ, and LZ votes for WM, so they did tick each other. Therefore, the answer is B.\n\nWait, but let me check if there\'s any scenario where this isn\'t the case. Suppose that Li Zilu didn\'t vote for Wang Ming. Wait, but according to Li Zilu\'s condition, he must vote for all candidates except those with full votes. Since no candidate has a full vote (ZH didn\'t vote), Li Zilu must vote for everyone. Therefore, he must vote for Wang Ming. So that\'s fixed.\n\nTherefore, the only way is that they both voted for each other, so B is correct.\n\nWait, but let me check the options again:\n\nOptions:\n\nA) Wang and Li didn\'t tick each other\n\nB) They did tick each other\n\nC) Wang chose Li but Li didn\'t choose Wang\n\nD) Wang didn\'t choose Li but Li did\n\nSo according to the above reasoning, B is correct. But let me see if there\'s a different interpretation.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the condition for Wang Ming is that he only votes for the same candidates that the voters who chose Zhao Jie voted for. Wait, perhaps "Wang Ming checked all those who checked Zhao Jie" means that if a voter checked Zhao Jie, then Wang Ming must check that voter\'s choices. Wait, but voters are people, not candidates. So maybe it\'s a mistranslation. Alternatively, perhaps "checked all those who checked Zhao Jie" refers to candidates that were checked by voters who checked Zhao Jie. So, for any candidate that was checked by a voter who checked Zhao Jie, Wang Ming must check that candidate.\n\nTherefore, if any voter (other than Wang Ming) voted for Zhao Jie and candidate X, then Wang Ming must vote for X. Additionally, since those voters also voted for Zhao Jie, Wang Ming must vote for Zhao Jie as well.\n\nSince Li Zilu voted for Zhao Jie and all other candidates (since he votes for everyone), then Wang Ming must vote for all the candidates that Li Zilu voted for along with Zhao Jie. Since Li Zilu voted for all three, Wang Ming must vote for all three.\n\nTherefore, Wang Ming voted for Li Zilu, and Li Zilu voted for Wang Ming, so B is correct.\n\nHmm, so I think the answer is B.\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
