hus, they both voted for each other, so B is correct.\n\nTherefore, the initial thought of C was incorrect. The correct answer should be B.\n\nWait, but the user initially thought C. Maybe I made a mistake in assuming that Wang Ming must vote for Li Zilu. Let's see:\n\nSuppose Wang Ming's condition is that he votes for all the candidates that anyone who voted for Zhao Jie also voted for.\n\nLi Zilu voted for Zhao Jie and Wang Ming and Li Zilu. So any of those (except Zhao Jie) must be included by Wang Ming.\n\nAdditionally, if another voter (say, someone else) voted for Zhao Jie and Wang Ming, then Wang Ming must include Wang Ming.\n\nBut since Li Zilu's vote includes Wang Ming, Wang Ming must include Wang Ming and Li Zilu.\n\nTherefore, Wang Ming does vote for Li Zilu.\n\nHence, B is correct.\n\nI think my reasoning holds, so the answer should be B.\n</think>\n\nThe problem involves determining the voting behavior of Wang Ming and Li Zilu based on the given conditions. Here's the step-by-step analysis:\n\n1. **Zhang Hao's Vote**: He did not vote for any candidate, meaning no candidate received a \"full vote\" (i.e., votes from all voters).\n\n2. **Li Zilu's Condition**: Li Zilu voted for all candidates who did not receive a full vote. Since Zhang Hao abstained, **no candidate could have a full vote**, so Li Zilu voted for **all candidates**. This means Li Zilu must have voted for Wang Ming (assuming Wang Ming is a candidate).\n\n3. **Wang Ming's Condition**: Wang Ming voted for all candidates that were voted for by any voter who also voted for Zhao Jie. Since Li Zilu voted for Zhao Jie **and** Wang Ming (among others), Wang Ming must include Wang Ming and Li Zilu in his votes. Thus, Wang Ming also voted for Li Zilu.\n\n4. **Conclusion**: Both Wang Ming and Li Zilu voted for each other.\n\n### Final Answer\n**B) Wang ming and li zilu tick each other**",
