ts unless explicitly stated otherwise.  \n- **C (Average Tax Payments):** This provides a broad average but doesn\u2019t isolate the top 10% or account for how the AMT specifically alters their tax liability.  \n- **D (Other Cities\u2019 Revenue):** Other cities\u2019 experiences may not reflect Carina\u2019s specific economic conditions, deductions, or income levels, making this a less direct comparison.\n\nThus, **Option B** is the most important to determine whether the AMT would increase revenue and be profitable for Carina. \n\n**Answer:** B",
